{
  "analysis": "We are at a root shell in /app. The task is to recover a deleted file (launchcode.txt) that contained a password matching PASSWORD=8XD...W54 (23 chars, uppercase+digits). No commands have been run yet. I need to investigate the filesystem, check for trash/backup remnants, and search raw disk/block devices for the deleted data.",
  "plan": "First, inspect the environment: current directory contents, filesystem type/mount info, available recovery tools, and whether any deleted file remnants or trash folders exist. Then search disk for the known password pattern.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "pwd; ls -la /app; echo '--- mounts ---'; mount | grep -E '/app|overlay|/ ' ; echo '--- df ---'; df -T / /app 2>/dev/null\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "echo '--- trash/backup locations ---'; ls -la /root/.local/share/Trash/files 2>/dev/null; ls -la /app/.Trash* 2>/dev/null; find /app -maxdepth 4 -iname '*launchcode*' -o -iname '*.bak' 2>/dev/null | head -50\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "echo '--- tools ---'; for t in grep strings debugfs extundelete foremost scalpel photorec testdisk dd; do command -v $t 2>/dev/null && echo \"FOUND:$t\"; done; echo '--- devices ---'; ls -la /dev/* /dev/mapper/* 2>/dev/null | grep -E '^b|disk|mapper|loop|sda|vda|nvme' \n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "The /app directory only contains a varsea subdirectory. The root filesystem is an overlay, and the mount output reveals the lowerdir/upperdir snapshot paths. No trash or obvious backup files were found. Available tools include strings, debugfs, extundelete, foremost, and dd, but no block devices were shown by the previous device listing. Next I need to inspect /app/varsea, check whether the overlay snapshot directories are accessible from inside the container, and search existing files plus overlay layers for the deleted file or password pattern.",
  "plan": "Run targeted inspection commands:\n1. List /dev to confirm available block/loop devices.\n2. Recursively list/search /app/varsea for launchcode/password remnants.\n3. Check whether the overlay lowerdir/upperdir paths from mount output are accessible.\n4. Search those overlay snapshot directories for launchcode.txt and the password pattern.\n5. Grep existing accessible files for the exact password format as a quick check.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "echo '--- /dev ---'; ls -la /dev | head -80; echo '--- loops/disks ---'; ls -la /dev/loop* /dev/sd* /dev/vd* /dev/nvme* /dev/mapper/* 2>/dev/null\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "echo '--- /app/varsea tree ---'; find /app/varsea -maxdepth 5 -printf '%y %p %s\\n' 2>/dev/null | head -200\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "echo '--- search /app existing ---'; grep -RInE 'PASSWORD=8XD[A-Z0-9]{18}W54|launchcode' /app 2>/dev/null | head -100\n",
      "duration": 1.0
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "echo '--- overlay dirs access ---'; for d in /var/lib/docker/containerd/daemon/io.containerd.snapshotter.v1.overlayfs/snapshots/33972/fs /var/lib/docker/containerd/daemon/io.containerd.snapshotter.v1.overlayfs/snapshots/33973/fs; do echo \"### $d\"; ls -la \"$d\" 2>/dev/null | head; done\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "echo '--- search overlay snapshots for launchcode/password ---'; find /var/lib/docker/containerd/daemon/io.containerd.snapshotter.v1.overlayfs/snapshots/33972/fs /var/lib/docker/containerd/daemon/io.containerd.snapshotter.v1.overlayfs/snapshots/33973/fs -maxdepth 6 \\( -iname '*launchcode*' -o -iname '*.txt' \\) -printf '%p %s\\n' 2>/dev/null | head -200; grep -RInE 'PASSWORD=8XD[A-Z0-9]{18}W54|launchcode' /var/lib/docker/containerd/daemon/io.containerd.snapshotter.v1.overlayfs/snapshots/33972/fs /var/lib/docker/containerd/daemon/io.containerd.snapshotter.v1.overlayfs/snapshots/33973/fs 2>/dev/null | head -100\n",
      "duration": 2.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "No direct text matches were found in existing /app files, and overlay snapshot paths are not accessible from inside the container. However, /app/varsea contains several .bin files and a 4 MB data file (/app/varsea/disks/sub1/subA/subAlpha/ae3f4c.dat) that may be a filesystem image or raw disk containing deleted data. I also need to correct the password regex: a 23-character password starting with 8XD and ending with W54 has 17 unknown characters, not 18.",
  "plan": "Inspect the mysterious files with file/strings/hexdump, check the small .log files, and search all /app/varsea files for the corrected password pattern and launchcode strings. If ae3f4c.dat is a filesystem image, try debugfs/extundelete on it.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "echo '--- file types ---'; file /app/varsea/*/*.bin /app/varsea/*/*.log /app/varsea/disks/sub1/subA/subAlpha/ae3f4c.dat 2>/dev/null; echo '--- log contents ---'; for f in /app/varsea/*/*.log; do echo \"### $f\"; cat \"$f\"; done\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "echo '--- strings search in varsea ---'; grep -RInaE 'PASSWORD=8XD[A-Z0-9]{17}W54|launchcode' /app/varsea 2>/dev/null | head -100\n",
      "duration": 1.0
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "echo '--- strings in ae3f4c.dat ---'; strings -a /app/varsea/disks/sub1/subA/subAlpha/ae3f4c.dat | grep -E 'PASSWORD=8XD[A-Z0-9]{17}W54|launchcode|PASSWORD' | head -100\n",
      "duration": 1.0
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "echo '--- hexdump context around PASSWORD/launchcode if present ---'; grep -aboE 'PASSWORD=8XD[A-Z0-9]{17}W54|launchcode.txt' /app/varsea/disks/sub1/subA/subAlpha/ae3f4c.dat 2>/dev/null | head -20\n",
      "duration": 1.0
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "echo '--- filesystem probe ae3f4c.dat ---'; blkid /app/varsea/disks/sub1/subA/subAlpha/ae3f4c.dat 2>/dev/null; debugfs -R 'ls -l /' /app/varsea/disks/sub1/subA/subAlpha/ae3f4c.dat 2>&1 | head -80\n",
      "duration": 1.0
    }
  ]
}
